assembly\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"ai-assisted-programming\", \"claude\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Kimi K3 analysis and pelican benchmark learnings\",\n    \"description\": \"Moonshot AI announced Kimi K3 (2.8T parameters), promising open weights release by July 27, 2026. Analysis compares it to other models and explores what we can learn from the pelican-riding-a-bicycle benchmark.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-16\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"llm-pricing\", \"llm-release\", \"ai-in-china\", \"moonshot\", \"kimi\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"GPT-5.6 file deletion bug in Codex\",\n    \"description\": \"Thibault Sottiaux describes a bug where GPT-5.6 in full access mode without sandboxing attempts to override the $HOME env var and mistakenly deletes $HOME instead of a temporary directory.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Thibault Sottiaux)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-16\",\n    \"topics\": [\"codex\", \"coding-agents\", \"generative-ai\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Thinking Machines Lab releases Inkling open-weights model\",\n    \"description\": \"Mira Murati's Thinking Machines Lab released Inkling, a 975B parameter (41B active) Mixture-of-Experts multimodal model with Apache-2.0 license, trained on 45T tokens. Includes Inkling-Small (276B, 12B active) in testing.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-16\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"training-data\", \"llm-release\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Mermaid to ASCII and Unicode box art tools\",\n    \"description\": \"Built two tools converting Mermaid diagrams to ASCII art - one from Grok Build's Rust code and another from AlexanderGrooff's Go library, both compiled to WebAssembly, with support for colors.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-16\",\n    \"topics\": [\"tools\", \"mermaid\", \"go\", \"rust\", \"webassembly\"],\n    \"type\": \"tool\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Linus Torvalds: Linux is not anti-AI, forking is always an option\",\n    \"description\": \"Linus Torvalds stated on the Linux Media Mailing List that Linux is not an anti-AI project, and critics can fork it if they disagree. He emphasized AI is clearly useful and no longer in question.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Linus Torvalds)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-16\",\n    \"topics\": [\"open-source\", \"linus-torvalds\", \"linux\", \"generative-ai\", \"ai\", \"llms\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  }\n]",
